For both semicircles, $r^2=25$, so $r=5$.

(a) The positive square root gives the upper semicircle. Its endpoints are $(-5,0)$ and $(5,0)$, and its highest point is $(0,5)$.
Domain: $[-5,5]$. Range: $[0,5]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-6,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1)--(0,6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue] (5,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=25mm];
\fill[black] (-5,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\fill[black] (5,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\fill[black] (0,5) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\path (-5,0) node[below] {$-5$} (5,0) node[below] {$5$} (0,5) node[above left] {$5$} (0,0) node[below left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b) The negative square root gives the lower semicircle. Its endpoints are $(-5,0)$ and $(5,0)$, and its lowest point is $(0,-5)$.
Domain: $[-5,5]$. Range: $[-5,0]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-6,0)--(6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->,black] (0,-6)--(0,1) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,curveblue] (-5,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=25mm];
\fill[black] (-5,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\fill[black] (5,0) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\fill[black] (0,-5) circle[radius=1.5pt];
\path (-5,0) node[above] {$-5$} (5,0) node[above] {$5$} (0,-5) node[below left] {$-5$} (0,0) node[above left] {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For both semicircles, $r^2=9$, so $r=3$. Their endpoints are $(0,-3)$ and $(0,3)$.

(a) Since $x\geq0$, draw the right semicircle. Its $x$-intercept is $(3,0)$.
